 "source_url": "https://github.com/randomparity/hmc-mcp/issues/1072",
 "claim_summary": "The release probe (_probe_released) runs on a free vterm slot of a not-activated partition. Arm `cost` alternates the probe's own teardown: `eof` (branch code: close the sealed stdin pipe's write end, read to stream end) and `rmvterm` (the pre-#1072 teardown: connection closed plus rmvterm, forced by making the EOF helper return False). Each `eof` probe received ' The write socket has closed. Exiting.\\n' 10.1 s after EOF, its stream ended on an open connection, it issued no rmvterm, and it took 11.60-11.63 s; each `rmvterm` probe took 3.13-3.16 s. Arm `race`: probe P starts, and client B retries ConsoleSession.open() until it acquires; every attempt while P held found the vterm held, B acquired 2.9 s after P's mkvterm exited, P issued no rmvterm, B's stream stayed open and silent for 8 s, an independent probe C found the vterm held and issued no rmvterm, and B's own close released it with no rmvterm in 21.89 s. Every run starts and ends with the partition Not Activated and the console slot free (baseline, restore-check probes).",
